always come down in a gaggle all together they pick you up and you go up together to a conference room after the power point we head down to the factory floor industrial spaces with 20 25 30 000 workers in a single enormous space they can exert a kind of eerie fascination there's a beauty to industrialization on such a massive scale you don't have to deny it there's a wonder to seeing so much order laid out in front of you and people are walking around whispering statistics in your ear it's easy to slip into a kind of stalinist wet dream i just try to subvert that by locking on to actual faces as they take me up and down the aisles, and the first thing I notice is the silence.
太安静了。

